# Chapter 1: A View of Strata.  The chapter is kept in four sources that
# this file reads: the elements of a document and the formats (view1), the
# screen and the panels (view2), the keys and the menus (view3) and the
# tools (view4).
.doc A View of Strata
.chapter 1
.h1 A View of Strata [view]
.ix Strata, overview
.ix Editor
.ix Document Manager
.ix Conventions of this manual
.ix Terminal version
.ix X11 version
Strata is a system for writing and printing technical documents: letters,
reports, proposals and manuals.  It has four programs: the Editor, the
Document Manager, the Printer and the Viewer.  A document is built from four
elements: text, blocks, columns and sections.

This chapter defines the elements, describes the screen of the Editor and the
ways to give it commands, and describes each program.  The other chapters use
the terms and the keys that this chapter defines.  Each key is listed twice,
by what it does and by the layer it belongs to (function key, menu,
accelerator).

.table 26 34
